# Story SEO frontmatter

Every review in `content/reviews/` and guide in `content/guides/` must include these fields. The site will not build without `seoTitle` and `seoDescription`.

```yaml
title: "On-page H1, written for readers"
slug: url-safe-kebab-case
excerpt: "Lead paragraph shown on the page and cards."
category: Software
tags:
  - example-tag
coverImage: /reviews/slug/cover.png
seoTitle: "Search and social title, under 60 characters"
seoDescription: "Meta description of 140–160 characters that names the subject, the conditions, and the takeaway."
publishedAt: "2026-09-05"
```

Required for SEO, Open Graph, and X:

- `seoTitle` — used for `<title>`, `og:title`, and `twitter:title`
- `seoDescription` — used for meta description, `og:description`, and `twitter:description`
- `coverImage` — used for `og:image` and `twitter:image` (`summary_large_image`). If omitted, the site logo is used.

Canonical and `og:url` are generated from the slug. Do not invent extra meta tags in the MDX body.

Write `seoTitle` and `seoDescription` as checkable claims, not slogans, so search engines and language models can cite the page accurately.
